Z||000000||fieroshop||12-17-1999||11:27 PM||||This morning hoping to get a smog certificate I had a head on collission with a gal speading down the street. Since I was pulling out of the driveway I guess it will be against me. What bothers me most is that now I have another parts car and this 86 restored SE that I had sold is no longer going to be on the road and will not get to see it's new owner.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Sage||12-17-1999||11:37 PM||||Really sorry to hear of your misfortune.  Hope noone was hurt.  It's times like this that you have to stop and take a look at the important things.  No matter who you are, where you live, how much money you have, or what you believe, it can all be gone in a split second.  The strongest arguement there is (in my mind) to be civil, considerate, and helpful to each other whenever we have the opportunity.  Hope some good comes out of it for you.  You have a whole new set of parts available now, that you didn't have before.  That's something!||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||12-17-1999||11:59 PM||||Fieroshop, I hope your ok. Ditto what Sage said, he's right about how fast it can be gone. I don't understand why it's your fault if she was speeding and you were backing out of a driveway??<P>PS. can the car be saved? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieroshop||12-18-1999||12:08 AM||||DXR_DAD no it can't be repaired but I do have another SE in stock and I will restored that one for my customer. Unfortunatly she is a little upset at not getting her car tommorrow and as far as being hurt my head hurts and has a big lump on my forehead, other than that I OK and so was the other driver.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-18-1999||01:25 AM||||DXR_DAD-No one can prove she was speeding (I assume), but it was obvious fieroshop was backing out of his driveway (can I assume that, too?).  Besides, she had the right-of-way.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||12-18-1999||09:11 AM||||Actually, he did not say he was backing out. He said he had a head on collision. It depends where the accident happened. If he pulled out into her lane, then he will probably be charged as being at fault and failing to yield the right of way. If he was completely in his lane and she crossed the center line and hit him, she would be at fault. I guess it is possible that he backed out, then once out in the street she hit him head on. Again, it would depend what lane everyone was in. Regardless, it sucks.||||reg||1
